    {
      "id": "grade",
      "name": "WIDOW'S GRADE",
      "tag": "DOC",
      "image": "/assets/lake-ulysses/backgrounds/prologue-lake.svg",
      "beats": [
        {
          "text": "WIDOW'S GRADE.\nEleven miles of two-lane between the high desert and the lake. Locals just call it the lake road.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "trout_dad",
              "text": "my dad wont drive it at night"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "No guardrail on the cliff side until 2009. The county called it a budget priority.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "jessrn",
              "text": "budget priority lmaooo"
            },
            {
              "who": "nightcrawler",
              "text": "bob voted no on that btw"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "speaker": "TRUCKER (RET.)",
          "text": "You see lights down there sometimes. Down in the wash. Nobody's car is down there anymore.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "lakelady",
              "text": "chills"
            },
            {
              "who": "dusty_ray",
              "text": "its the reflectors from the old wrecks"
            },
            {
              "who": "jessrn",
              "text": "no its not"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Since 1974, the Grade has taken thirty-one lives. Most of them were young. Most of them were leaving.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "nightcrawler",
              "text": "leaving where"
            },
            {
              "who": "trout_dad",
              "text": "everybody leaves this town eventually"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Caleb, nineteen. His car was found in the morning, past the third switchback.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "jessrn",
              "text": "i went to school with him"
            },
            {
              "who": "lakelady",
              "text": "his mom still goes to every service"
            },
            {
              "who": "dusty_ray",
              "text": "rip"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "speaker": "DEPUTY (RET.)",
          "text": "The kids who go off up there, they're never driving toward anything. You learn that.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "nightcrawler",
              "text": "..."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Some families put up crosses. The county takes them down every spring. Somebody always puts them back.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "trout_dad",
              "text": "my aunt puts one up every year"
            },
            {
              "who": "jessrn",
              "text": "the one with the church ribbon is still there"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Next time: the lights in the wash. Who's driving?",
          "holdMs": 4000,
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "lakelady",
              "text": "NEXT TIME??"
            },
            {
              "who": "dusty_ray",
              "text": "@{handle} you ever seen the lights?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pastor",
      "name": "THE LIVING WATER HOUR",
      "tag": "PUBLIC ACCESS",
      "beats": [
        {
          "speaker": "PASTOR GABRIEL",
          "text": "Good evening, Lake Ulysses, and welcome to The Living Water Hour! Brought to you by Baiter's Bait & Tackle.",
          "comments": [
            {
              "who": "lakelady",
              "text": "the same bob??"
